<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - April 10.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - April 10.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for April 10.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Apr    208.00    212.50    213.50     224.50</p>
<p>    May    208.00    212.50    213.50     224.50</p>
<p>    Jun    203.00    207.50    205.50     221.00</p>
<p>    Jul    200.00    204.50    205.50     218.50</p>
<p>    Aug    199.00    203.50    204.50     217.50</p>
<p>    Sept   199.00    203.50    204.50     217.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased A$2.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	178.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  153.50	    Port Adelaide	 155.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     153.75	    Port Giles	    155.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	151.50	    Wallaroo		153.50</p>
<p>    New South Wales		   Port Pirie	    150.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     153.50	    Port Lincoln	  156.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   154.00	    Thevenard	     151.75</p>
<p>    Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 153.00	     Esperance	    158.25</p>
<p>    Portland	154.00	     Albany		 159.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    161.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    159.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Summer Time (0530 GMT).  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
